From bda8cc6b50bde7b111c77f77dbac7be7a384a887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneup03 <oneup03@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:01:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Add RECOMP_NO_MODS to build without the mod system

The mod loader needs dynamic loading, page protection, a live recompiler
and a 16 MB region of RDRAM, none of which a 3DS has (mods.cpp already
refuses 32-bit ARM). With the option on, the mod sources are left out,
the recomp.cpp wrappers over ModContext and the mod-loading step in
wait_for_game_started are compiled out, and mods_stub.cpp supplies the
few entry points the rest of the runtime still calls.

The recompiled patches call recomp_trigger_event for every declared
event, and the real one quick-exits unless load_mods sized its callback
table, so the stub makes it a no-op.
